Title: Petition to save historic sea pool reaches 1,000 signatures
Date: 2025-07-14
Firsthand information: {'Speaker': [{'Speaker': 'Petition organiser Nina Zaech', 'Text': 'Petition organiser Nina Zaech described the pool as a "vital piece of Jersey\'s heritage" that could support health, leisure, and tourism.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 4, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 119}}], 'Description': [{'Description': 'A petition to restore the 128-year-old Victoria Marine Lake in St Helier has reached 1,000 signatures.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 1, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 82}}, {'Description': "The level of interest, external means there will now be a response from Jersey's government.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 2, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 92}}, {'Description': 'Campaigners, including the newly-formed Save Our Pool Working Group, are calling for urgent restoration.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 4, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 97}}, {'Description': 'A 2024 inspection found the pool required "comprehensive work".', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 5, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 56}}, {'Description': 'Last month, Infrastructure Minister Andy Jehan was asked how the site would be maintained and said repairs would be "uneconomical" due to planned sea defence upgrades along the waterfront.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 6, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 174}}], 'Image': [{'ID': 'image_1', 'Caption': 'A sea pool with a horseshoe shape barrier on a beach with houses behind.'}]}
